  "review": {
    "peak_dependency": "Native reconstruction changes peak/background state but not stripped intensity: exact full-array comparisons for 4 spectra x 3 action variants. No peak search is required inside the C++ stripping kernel; downstream derived state is invalidated.",
    "radiation": "Captured identical output for Cu custom 1.54056, Mo .71073, neutron, electron, unknown rad. Native ignores these metadata; product explicitly restricts fixed Cu model.",
    "repeated": "Native applies subtraction again despite existing flag; C++ rejects repeated and unknown history.",
    "negative": "Negative outputs observed for all three measured patterns; preserve finite negatives, no clipping.",
    "boundary": "High-angle case has 391 NaN intensities; preserve transcript as historical evidence. Product rejects invalid inverse-sine domain. Single/duplicate/descending are unsupported irrespective of finite native transcript.",
    "harness": "First run without native GUI sinks crashed at no-window presentation callback. Retained separately; corrected capture wraps presentation only, unchanged numerical modules.",
    "parameters": "Fixed istog=3 weights [-.152766460,-.268687600,-.110173100], levers [1.002353500,1.002453600,1.002578830]. No configurable wavelength or ratio inside native kernel; nominal Cu doublet 2:1 is a product precondition, not a replacement coefficient formula.",
    "arithmetic": "Subtract global minimum, scan ascending source bins, skip negative current bins, distribute three signed corrections linearly to bracketing half-angle bins using mutated intensity. First unavailable upper bracket exits the whole scan; add minimum back. Native last bin is excluded as an upper interpolation bracket."
  },
